## 2. Agent Type Comparison

| Dimension | RUFUS v3 `@claude-flow/swarm` | SuperNEXUS `gemas_core` |
|-----------|-------------------------------|-------------------------|
| **Total roles** | 15 `AgentRole` enum members | 5 dedicated + 18 role-LLM = 23 |
| **Dedicated workers** | Conceptually 1 (the swarm) + 1 `queen-coordinator` | 5 hard-coded: `ayuda`, `scholar`, `sage`, `biblioteca`, `prompter` |
| **Role-LLM count** | n/a — all 15 are first-class `Agent` instances | 18 manifests (`code`, `architect`, `debugger`, `tester`, `security`, `devops`, etc.) |
| **Lifecycle states** | `idle / active / busy / paused / terminated / error` | Implicit in `dispatch_gema` return codes; not explicit field on `GemaBase` |
| **Identity** | `AgentId` (ULID), `SwarmId` | `gema.name` (string from manifest `name` field) |
| **Specialization source** | In-code `AgentRole` union + capabilities array | `GemaManifest.system_prompt` (declarative JSON) |
| **Topology** | `mesh / hierarchical / centralized / hybrid` (`TopologyType`) | None — flat dict `{gema_id: GemaBase}` |
| **DDD pattern** | Aggregate root, domain/infrastructure separation | `GemaBase` ABC + dataclass manifest (light DDD) |
| **Persistence** | Live `Agent` instances in `UnifiedSwarmCoordinator` | Disk: `data/gemas/*.json`; runtime: in-memory dict |
| **Cross-agent comms** | `MessageBus` (1000+ msg/s) with acks | `message_board.db` via `send_message` / `read_messages` MCP |
| **Roles missing in gemas_core** | `queen-coordinator`, `swarm-specialist`, `integration-architect`, `performance-engineer`, `core-architect`, `test-architect`, `project-coordinator`, `planner`, `researcher` | (Most overlap with existing `director`, `architect`, `code`, `tester`, `scholar`; `planner` and `integration-architect` are net-new) |
| **Roles unique to gemas_core** | — | `ayuda`, `scholar`, `sage`, `biblioteca`, `prompter` (dedicated Python workers), `music`, `vision` (Ollama-vision) |
| **Adding a new role** | TS class with `AgentRole` enum membership + `IAgentRegistry.register()` | Drop `data/gemas/<name>.json` + (optional) `workers/<name>.py` extending `GemaBase` |
| **Hot reload** | n/a (long-running Node process) | n/a (re-instantiate via `build_standard_gemas()` on restart) |

**Key insight:** RUFUS models agents as runtime objects inside a long-lived Node coordinator; gemas_core models them as **declarative + stateless + restart-safe**. The RUFUS `Agent` aggregate can be ported as a *runtime-side data structure* (e.g. an in-memory `GemaInstance` with `status`, `last_used_at`, `active_task_count`) without changing the public manifest/dispatch contract.

