## 6. Anti-Port List (do NOT port these)

| Source | Reason |
|--------|--------|
| `HybridBackend` implementation (sql.js + native HNSW binding) | Node.js-specific. SuperNEXUS already has `nexus_memory.db` (SQLite/FTS5) and `nomic-embed-text` (Ollama) — port the **routing strategy contract**, not the backend. |
| `RaftConsensus` (full impl) | Heavy ceremony, 3 timers (election/heartbeat/replicate), pluggable transport. SuperNEXUS already has NexusHive as a service-based coordination layer; Raft would be a second, competing system. **Port the *idea* of pluggable transport as a `Protocol` ABC if needed, not the full impl.** |
| `GossipConsensus` (full impl) | Bounded-set gossip with version propagation is useful in 100+ peer swarms. SuperNEXUS has 7 peers in a star topology; gossip is overkill. The pattern is already represented by `message_board.db` polling. |
| `MessageBus` + `Deque` circular buffer (1000+ msg/s target) | The 7-peer NexusHive is not throughput-bound; 1000 msg/s is irrelevant. The `Deque` data structure exists in Python's `collections.deque` — if needed, just use that. |
| The full `@claude-flow/hooks` runtime | TypeScript `EventEmitter`-based hook executor with 19 events + 5 priorities + 4 daemons. SuperNEXUS has `plan_mode` and 1 priority level. Port the *enums* (small win) and the *idea* of priority levels, but do not port the runtime. |
| `ReasoningBank` (full impl) | Vector-based pattern learning is conceptually already in `self_learning_loop.py`. Adding ReasoningBank as a second pattern-learner would create a parallel pipeline that drift over time. |
| `queen-coordinator` / `TopologyManager` role-based caches | The queen pattern is for 100+ agent swarms. SuperNEXUS has 23 gemas in a flat dict — `O(1)` role-based indexes are a YAGNI optimization. |
| `SwarmHub` → `UnifiedSwarmCoordinator` facade | ADR-003 marks it deprecated. Port the deprecated pattern is a net negative. |
| `safeNum` cross-language port | Python's `decimal.Decimal` + `pydantic` validation is the idiomatic equivalent. Don't port the TS coercion; just use stdlib. |
| Any TypeScript decorator or `Reflect.metadata` | Python has its own `functools.wraps` / `pydantic` model_validator idioms; copying TS-specific reflection patterns is a transliteration anti-pattern. |
| The full `teammate-plugin` package | Same Claude Code version coupling. The *contract* (PeerStatus, MailboxMessage, PlanProposal) is the only thing with cross-language value. |
| `GNN` integration (`ruvector/gnn.ts`) | Requires `ruvector` native binding. SuperNEXUS has no equivalent vector DB beyond Ollama embeddings. |
| `ruvector/self-learning.ts` | Same native-binding constraint. |
| `memory-initializer.ts` + `memory-bridge.ts` | Bootstrap code for the AgentDB CLI runtime — N/A in SuperNEXUS. |

**Rule of thumb:** port the **enums**, the **contracts**, and the **algorithms** (pluggable functions). Never port the **runtime plumbing** that holds those contracts together — every language has its own idioms, and SuperNEXUS already has a runtime.

